br.br:
1.    A method for providing assistance during gameplay, comprising: 


accessing a profile model associated with a user account of a user, wherein the profile model is used to generate one or more predictive indicators based on a plurality of game contexts of one or more games; 


receiving a request for accessing a game for a game session via the user account; 


generating assistance input for the user responsive to the one or more predictive indicators that the user will be unable to complete a task in the game, the task being associated to a game context, wherein the assistance input is provided before the user performs the task. 






2.    The method of claim 1, wherein the profile model includes a neural network that is trained by one or more gameplays occurring via the user account, the one or more gameplays used to perform labeling and classification of the plurality of game contexts, labeling and classification of user interactions, and labeling and classification of performance metrics.





3.    The method of claim 2, wherein said generating the assistance input occurs upon determining that the game context of the game session is similar to one or more of the plurality of game contexts used to train the profile model.





4.    The method of claim 2, further comprising: 


generating state data for the one or more gameplays; 


parsing the state data to identify the plurality of game contexts of the one or more games, the user interactions with the plurality of game contexts, and the performance metrics that are generated based on the user interactions and the plurality of game contexts. 






5.    The method of claim 4, further comprising: 


labeling the plurality of game contexts to identify the plurality of game contexts; 


labeling the user interactions to identify the user interactions; 


labeling the performance metrics to identify the performance metrics; 


classifying the game contexts to provide a level to each of the game contexts; 


classifying the user interactions to provide a level to each of the user interactions; and 

classifying the performance metrics to provide a level to each of the performance metrics.





6.    The method of claim 5, wherein the one or more predictive indicators are determined based on the levels of the game contexts, the levels of the interactions, and the levels of the performance metrics, a number of occurrences of the levels of the game contexts, a number of occurrences of the levels of the interactions, and a number of occurrences of the levels of the performance metrics.





7.    The method of claim 1, wherein the assistance input includes controller input data, light data for controlling one or more lights on a controller of the game, screen text data for presenting on a display device used during the game session, and audio data for outputting sounds during the game session.





8.    A computer system for providing assistance during gameplay, comprising: 


a processor configured to: 


access a profile model associated with a user account of a user, wherein the profile model is used to generate one or more predictive indicators based on a plurality of game contexts of one or more games; 


receive a request for accessing a game for a game session via the user account; 


generate assistance input for the user responsive to the one or more predictive indicators that the user will be unable to complete a task in the game, the task being associated to a game context; and 


provide the assistance input before the user performs the task; and 


a memory device coupled to the processor. 






9.    The computer system of claim 8, wherein the profile model includes a neural network that is trained by one or more gameplays occurring via the user account, the one or more gameplays used to perform labeling and classification of the plurality of game contexts, labeling and classification of user interactions, and labeling and classification of performance metrics.



10.   The computer system of claim 9, wherein the assistance input is generated when the profile model determines that a game context of the game session is similar to one of the plurality of game contexts used to train the profile model.





11.   The computer system of claim 9, wherein the processor is configured to: 


generate state data for the one or more gameplays; 


parse the state data to identify the plurality of game contexts of the one or more games, the user interactions with the plurality of game contexts, and performance metrics that are generated based on the user interactions and the plurality of game contexts. 






12.   The computer system of claim 11, wherein the processor is configured to: 


label the game contexts to identify the plurality of game contexts; 


label the user interactions by the user to identify the user interactions; 


label the performance metrics to identify the performance metrics; 


classify the plurality of game contexts to provide a level to each of the plurality of game contexts; 


classify the user interactions to provide a level to each of the user interactions; and 


classify the performance metrics to provide a level to each of the performance metrics. 






13.   The computer system of claim 12, wherein the one or more predictive indicators are determined based on the levels of the plurality of game contexts, the levels of the user interactions, and the levels of the performance metrics, a number of occurrences of the levels of the plurality of game contexts, a number of occurrences of the levels of the user interactions, and a number of occurrences of the levels of the performance metrics.





14.   The computer system of claim of claim 8, wherein the assistance input includes controller input data, light data for controlling one or more lights on a controller of the game, screen text data for presenting on a display device used during the game session, and audio data for outputting sounds during the game session.





15.   A system for providing assistance during gameplay, comprising: 


a client device; and 

a server coupled to the client device via a computer network, wherein the server is configured to: 


access a profile model associated with a user account of a user, wherein the profile model is used to generate one or more predictive indicators based on a plurality of game contexts of one or more games; 


receive a request for accessing a game for a game session via the user account; 


generate assistance input for the user responsive to the one or more predictive indicators that the user will be unable to complete a task in the game, the task being associated to a game context; and 


send the assistance input before the user performs the task, wherein the client device is configured to receive the assistance input from the server via the computer network. 






16.   The system of claim 15, wherein the assistance input is generated when the profile model determines that the game context of the game session is similar to one of the plurality of game contexts used to train the profile model.





17.   The system of claim 15, wherein the profile model includes a neural network that is trained by one or more gameplays occurring via the user account, the one or more gameplays used to perform labeling and classification of the plurality of game contexts, labeling and classification of user interactions, and labeling and classification of performance metrics.





18.   The system of claim 17, wherein the server is configured to: 


generate state data for the one or more gameplays; 


parse the state data to identify the plurality of game contexts of the one or more games, the user interactions with the plurality of game contexts, and the performance metrics that are generated based on the user interactions and the plurality of game contexts. 






19.   The system of claim 15, wherein the profile model is an artificial intelligence model, wherein the server is configured to: 


label the plurality of game contexts to identify the plurality of game contexts; 


label user interactions with the plurality of game contexts to identify the user interactions; 

label performance metrics achieved based on the user interactions to identify the performance metrics; 


classify the plurality of game contexts to provide a level to each of the plurality of game contexts; 


classify the user interactions to provide a level to each of the user interactions; 


classify the performance metrics to provide a level to each of the performance metrics, wherein the one or more predictive indicators are determined based on the levels of the plurality of game contexts, the levels of the user interactions, and the levels of the performance metrics, a number of occurrences of the levels of the plurality of game contexts, a number of occurrences of the levels of the user interactions, and a number of occurrences of the levels of the performance metrics. 






20.    The system of claim 15, wherein the client device is a hand-held controller or a head- mounted display.
